build: 2026-06-24 v10.76.17 (STABILITY: the real launch fix — erase the fullscreen cover from body metadata)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
notesT: THIS is the actual launch fix (10.76.14/.15/.16 all black-screened; .15/.16 fixed
  real-but-secondary bugs). Root cause: a SwiftUI type-metadata STACK OVERFLOW (SIGSEGV)
  at launch — a compile-clean crash, no Swift trap, just black screen. EchoelStudioView is
  mounted at launch (WorkspaceView keeps all surfaces in a ZStack). Its `.fullScreenCover`
  content (`visualCoverContent` — the immersive ZStack with the VJ overlay + analytics
  overlay + MetalBioView) was NOT type-erased, and since `.fullScreenCover` is generic over
  its content type, that whole deep nesting got baked into the view's `body` type metadata.
  When 10.76.10 (Bio→Visual) and 10.76.11 (analytics overlay) GREW that cover, the body
  metadata crossed the decoder's recursion limit → overflow → SIGSEGV at launch. That's why
  10.76.9 launched (verified) but everything from 10.76.10 on bricked, and why the sheet-
  consolidation (.15) and the no-auto-modal fix (.16) didn't help — neither touched the
  cover's contribution to body. FIX: wrap every `.fullScreenCover` branch in AnyView (it was
  already done for the 16 `.sheet` cases and the body sections) so the deep cover type leaves
  body's metadata. MTKView identity preserved (stable wrapped type → updateUIView, no
  teardown). Reviewed twice (ui-state + launch-path audit): sufficient, compiles under
  -warnings-as-errors. No feature changes — same visual, same controls.
  INSTALL 10.76.17 from TestFlight. It should finally launch. If it still black-screens,
  send the crash log (Settings > Privacy & Security > Analytics & Improvements > Analytics
  Data > newest "Echoel..." entry) — a SIGSEGV in swift_getTypeByMangledName confirms this
  class of bug; anything else points elsewhere.
